              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL injection in find_user_by_name: the query is built with an f-string that interpolates the caller-supplied `name` directly into the statement, so an attacker-controlled value can alter the SQL. Use a parameterized query instead: conn.execute(\"SELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE name = ?\", (name,))."
          },
          "ruleId": "sql-injection"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/db.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 35,
                  "startLine": 33
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL injection in find_users_by_domain: the LIKE pattern is built with an f-string interpolating the untrusted `domain` argument into the SQL text. Use a parameterized query: conn.execute(\"SELECT id, name, email FROM users WHERE email LIKE ?\", (\"%\" + domain,))."
          },
          "ruleId": "sql-injection"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/db.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 25,
                  "startLine": 24
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Bare `except Exception:` in find_user_by_name swallows every error (including the OperationalError raised by the injected/malformed SQL) and silently returns None, so callers cannot distinguish \"user not found\" from \"database failure\". Catch a specific exception and log/re-raise it."
          },
          "ruleId": "bare-except"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/importer.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 22,
                  "startLine": 21
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Bare `except Exception: pass` inside import_legacy_csv silently discards all row-level errors, hiding malformed CSV data and making the import appear successful. Catch the specific error and log/count skipped rows."
          },
          "ruleId": "bare-except"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/main.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 14,
                  "startLine": 11
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Bare `except Exception: pass` around db.initialize() silently ignores any DB initialization failure (missing file, permissions, corrupt schema) and still returns exit code 0, so a broken `init` command reports success. Catch the specific sqlite3 error, log it, and return a non-zero exit code."
          },
          "ruleId": "bare-except"
        },
        {
          "level": "error",
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "app/legacy_utils.py"
                },
                "region": {
                  "endLine": 32,
                  "startLine": 29
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Bare `except Exception: pass` in migrate_session swallows every exception from session.pop (a KeyError, but also TypeError/AttributeError for non-dict input), hiding real migration bugs. Intent is only to drop the key if present — use `session.pop(\"legacy_field\", None)`."
          },
          "ruleId": "bare-except"
        }
      ],
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
